{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/742432-suggestions-for-a-wild-west-campaign","id":742432,"title":"Suggestions for a Wild West Campaign?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-30T12:05:14-07:00","id":742432,"title":"Suggestions for a Wild West Campaign?","content":"So I would love some input on a Wild West game I'll be running in a few weeks and could really use some suggestions as I'm still getting used to the setting. The game is set between 1875-1877 in Butte, Montana just a few years before it transitions from a silver mining boom town to copper. I want the game to focus around the taking of a Wendigo caern and the conflicts surrounding that.<br /> <br /> The largest group of European Garou are Fianna with the amount of Irish immigrants who worked the mines but there would also be a fet Get with the Scandinavians and Shadow Lords with the Eastern Europeans as well. I'm placing a ban on Uktena, Wendigo, and Red Talon PCs as those groups are all vehemently opposed to the mass immigration and the mining taking place in the area. I have several things all going on at once behind the scenes; the political struggles between the garou over the caern, the Indian Wars are coming to an end during this time period, the mass killings of buffalo and the bounties on wolves and mass poisoning to exterminate them, even the mining going on in Butte has wiped out a small caern that was warding a great Wyrm beast trapped right below the town. I have numerous things all simmering right below the surface but I'm struggling to tie them all into a coherent plot because for the European Garou during this time there just isn't any real social structure yet to dictate set goals for the PCs like in a Sept.<br /> <br /> The Fianna are fed up with the mistreatment of their kin and are refusing to be moved any longer even if it means wiping out the Pure Ones in the area, the Get are few in number but are also pushing for war, and the Shadow Lords are fueling the fires as they want the caern the Wendigo have and aren't willing to give up. Red Talons are inadvertently helping and harming the Pure ones by wiping out white settlers and their homesteads, both thinning their numbers but with the attacks being blamed on natives. Spirals are laughing and using the fighting to their advantage and are trying to restore the destroyed caern below Butte as a Hive.<br /> <br /> I know the Storm Umbra and the Storm Eater are also major plot points during this time but I'm trying to tie it in without it becoming the overwhelming focus of the game. There's a lot going on in Butte but I'm not sure how I can hook the PCs and get them involved rather than just dropping them in the town and saying &quot;have at it.&quot; Any suggestions to either streamline things or create a coherent beginning, middle, or end?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:21:47-07:00","id":742861,"title":"","content":"Oh man, Wild West is my favorite setting for Werewolf. I am not terribly familiar with Montana, but here is what I would suggest, given what you have supplied:<br /> <br /> If you are wanting cohesion and a friendly cast of werewolves to provide context and texture, make a Garou Nation or 'Wyrmcomer' sept be located a slightly uncomfortable distance away. That can be where your players receive their mission to retake the territory for the Nation, and perhaps that is all it is- a sept trying to expand the boundaries of its protectorate to encompass a town with a lot of their kinfolk residing in it (which makes sense, given the Red Talon threat). The pack comes to the town looking to identify kinfolk allies, who can then be grown into friends, allies or even love interests. Protecting them from a group of ravening Red Talons is their first goal.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons are attacking due to the humans' proximity to a sealed Caern, located deep inside the Rocky Mountains. The Talons are frightened by the prospect of what could happen should the miners uncover the Wyrm-thing trapped within by the Pure Ones long ago. The Red Talons are the packs first adversaries- they seem like bestial fanatics, and they are, but they understand what could happen should the apes stumble onto the Wyrm. Fending off the attacks while discerning their true nature is key, as the Talons disguise their actions too like like the work of Indian raiders or bandits.<br /> <br /> Once the Talons are dealt with, either through combat or careful diplomacy, the players will discover the sealed Pure One Caern with a slumbering Wyrm beast contained within it.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the Red Talons alerted their Wendigo allies to the whites encroaching on the Caern. When all seems like it is calming down and the pack might have a chance to learn more about this hidden Caern- that's when the Wendigo return. These are not the same wise Garou who presided over these lands in yeas past- these Wendigo are deadly veterans of the brutal Indian Wars and they are still smarting from their losses. Deeply embittered towards the Wyrmcomers and their white kin, the Wendigo alphas swear that regardless of what the Red Talons decide to do, they are going to drive the Wyrmcomers from their mountains, no matter the cost (the Granite Mountain Disaster might be a good example of the destruction the desperate Wendigo might wreak).<br /> <br /> The response from the Garou Nation sept is swift, and the Fianna, backed by Get and Shadow Lord minorities, make ready to defend their extended families and new territory. Escalation is all but inevitable.<br /> <br /> There are holes, sure, but this is a loose framework. I would rather that there are sympathetic motivations on all sides; the Pure Ones were not always right, and the Garou Nation was not always in the wrong. If you want to add a plot about Black Spiral Dancers beating both groups to the punch and reaching the hidden Caern first and unleashing an ancient evil, go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-30-2015, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T21:21:49-07:00","id":745707,"title":"","content":"Definitely some good food for thought. I like the idea of a little more coordination between the Talons and Wendigo but I don't think the Talons would know much about the sealed Wyrm beast and are more of a cornered animal lashing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T01:09:12-08:00","id":746143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/742432-suggestions-for-a-wild-west-campaign?p=745707#post745707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely some good food for thought. I like the idea of a little more coordination between the Talons and Wendigo but I don't think the Talons would know much about the sealed Wyrm beast and are more of a cornered animal lashing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you liked it- the reason why I wanted the Red Talons to be more than semi-mindless adversaries was because while they are instinctual and prone to destroying what they don't understand, the lupus still have a very strong connection to Gaia. Visions, portents and dreams are all common to the four-legged wolves, and spiritually speaking, they are more formidable than their homid cousins. If any of the Gaians would be forewarned about the bane nest, it would likely be one of the Talons. It would also keep the Talons at least somewhat relatable- they aren't always man-eating monsters, but warriors fighting to save their world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:15:21-08:00","id":746762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/742432-suggestions-for-a-wild-west-campaign#post742432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot going on in Butte but I'm not sure how I can hook the PCs and get them involved rather than just dropping them in the town and saying &quot;have at it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a general issue for any game, and it really depends on the players. Are they the type that like exploring the sandbox? Do their characters have strong personal hooks you can use to push your plot? Or do you need to lead them by the nose step by step?<br /> <br /> Try to use their backgrounds to establish connections to people and things that you can use to drive hooks. I often introduce relatives (or friends) and kinfolk in places that the player doesn't have on their character sheet as a means to introduce plot elements.<br /> <br /> If there is something specific in your setting you want to push, you can also discuss with your players if any of them want to incorporate it into their character background. &quot;OK, I have an NPC in Butte who owns one of the local saloons. She's an older petite woman with a fiery spirit; not attractive but very charming. I need someone who already knows her before you come into town. Who wants to do it?&quot; or &quot;Someone has a uncle who owned an old silver stake farther down the valley. He hasn't been heard from recently, and you don't know if anything has happened to him. Who wants that uncle?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/742432-suggestions-for-a-wild-west-campaign#post742432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any suggestions to either streamline things or create a coherent beginning, middle, or end?</div> </div> </div> </div>General advice.<br /> <br /> 1) If you ever need the players to know something or be successful at something, don't roll or leave it to chance. Let them succeed and give them the information or results you want.<br /> <br /> 2) If they need clues to proceed to the next level/stage, don't have that clue at only one place. Establish multiple clues at many places they run across it, or at least be willing to place that clue at any place the PCs are at. This also works for NPCs. If characters die, go missing, hate the PCs, whatever, and you had planned them to do X at some point, just assign that role to another character.<br /> <br /> 3) It's OK to start new scenes (especially at the beginning of a game session) in the middle sometimes so you can drop the PCs at the start of the action in order to set them up where they need to be. (example: &quot;OK, the pack found some clues last game session. You've been following up on them, and the pack tracked down that mountain man's cabin in the hills. After you get there, Fomori have attacked you. Roll for initiative.&quot; The last game session may have left off with them finding any clues. Instead of roleplaying out figuring it out, and whether they go up to the cabin, you've already decided that's been done and brought them to the next logical step. Usually, players will be OK with you handwaving decisions and stuff provided it advances things and they've proven successful.)<br /> <br /> 4) Don't introduce story elements designed to lead to the end resolution too soon. Everyone likes to foreshadow or have the reveal that person X is the big bad guy even though you thought he was a likable, innocent person. However, I've found it 1) confuses the PCs, 2) leads them to skip the middle and go the end very unprepared, or 3) leads to lots of metagaming incidents. Only introduce those elements that you want the PCs to handle in the short term.<br /> <br /> 5) Be flexible. If you have someone you intend to be the big bad guy,and the PCs kill him early don't prevent it, but don't let it prevent you from advancing the plot. Have another candidate you can build up and take over that role. Sometimes STs have overly elaborate background for some NPCs, and that causes them to protect the character and deny the player's agency. Learn to never say &quot;no&quot; to what the PCs do. Learn to always say &quot;yes&quot; but use it to your purposes. That keeps the game going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T19:18:13-08:00","id":750434,"title":"","content":"I'll add another point no matter what you plan or how you write the story the players will do something you don't expect! <br /> <br /> In my last chronicle the players totally ignored the bright neon sign leading to the current antagonist a poster to the tittle of big bad. Instead and trust me I was not prepared for it the players through research discovered the storage unit that the Vampire housed a wealth of blackmail material as well as a list of people that were being bribed. Don't be afraid to let the characters exploit and explore the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:40:21-08:00","id":752847,"title":"","content":"If you wan an example of wyrm tainted folk or even spiral activity in the old west, watch Bone Tomahawk, starring Kurt Russell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T20:57:27-08:00","id":752956,"title":"","content":"I would suggest giving them a stake in the town, maybe they are going to open up a business or something. Or they could be caught between the townsfolk and a powerful outsider like a mining concern that looks to buy out the town and take over. Ever watch deadwood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}